<%# The way into Test Mode for whoever is holding a LIVE play link — a
    facilitator demoing the Verto at an event, a creator checking it on a real
    phone, a partner walking a funder through it. Their run shouldn't land in
    the results, and until now their only options were to pollute them or to go
    back to the studio for a different link.

    It has to be here, in the respondent's player, and it has to be impossible
    to reach by accident: anyone with the public link can find it, and a
    respondent who trips into it would have their real answers silently
    discarded. So: no label, no visible affordance, and two deliberate acts.
    Press and hold the (invisible) hotspot for TEST_HOLD_MS to arm the confirm
    chip, then tap the chip within TEST_ARM_MS. Sliding off, letting go early,
    or simply waiting all disarm it. Same arm/disarm shape as the editor's
    delete button (type_panel_controller.js#delete), for the same reason.

    Nothing here can WRITE anything — the worst a respondent who finds it can
    do is decline to submit, which closing the tab already achieves. That is why
    it needs no owner setting and no token.

    aria-hidden on the hotspot is deliberate: a hidden affordance announced by a
    screen reader isn't hidden. The equivalent for anyone who can't perform the
    gesture is the URL itself (/test/live/:token), which is a plain link. The
    chip, once armed, IS announced — by then it's a real button with a real
    label. %>
<span class="test-hatch-hotspot" aria-hidden="true"
      data-action="pointerdown->player#testHoldStart
                   pointermove->player#testHoldMove
                   pointerup->player#testHoldCancel
                   pointerleave->player#testHoldCancel
                   pointercancel->player#testHoldCancel"></span>
<%# title, not aria-label: the accessible name has to keep the visible label
    ("Start test mode") inside it, or voice control can't act on what it can
    see. The banner string is the description on top of that name, not a
    replacement for it — and the ⚗ is hidden because it is a mark, not a word. %>
<button type="button" class="test-hatch-confirm" hidden
        data-player-target="testConfirm"
        title="<%= t("player.test_mode_banner") %>"
        data-action="click->player#enterTestMode">
  <span aria-hidden="true">⚗</span> <%= t("player.test_mode_enter") %>
</button>
